WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.704
Priya: Just to recap, the first slice passed. Additional malformed-data tests will carry over separately.

2
00:00:07.704 --> 00:00:16.344
Hannah: The agreed acceptance criteria are met. The extra cases extend coverage beyond those fixtures.

3
00:00:16.344 --> 00:00:23.807
Raj: Full extraction was a stretch, as expected. Just to confirm, no production release yet, right?

4
00:00:23.807 --> 00:00:32.063
Anika: Right, consumer sign-off covers isolated report comparisons. Operational release still needs its own approval.

5
00:00:32.063 --> 00:00:38.759
Lukas: What made review easier this iteration? We should preserve the practices that actually helped.

6
00:00:38.759 --> 00:00:46.799
Raj: Small changes and fixed fixtures helped most. Maybe discovery deserves an earlier owner next time.

7
00:00:46.799 --> 00:00:55.823
Hannah: Agreed, waiting for samples delayed meaningful feedback. We shouldn't blame implementation for every delay.

8
00:00:55.823 --> 00:01:03.166
Priya: One action item is tracking sample dependencies. We'll compare waiting time in the next iteration.

9
00:01:03.166 --> 00:01:10.366
Lukas: Faster local tests are a useful result. They don't prove production reliability has improved yet.

10
00:01:10.366 --> 00:01:18.550
Anika: Good distinction, I'll keep that in the summary. Today's evidence supports maintainability, not outage reduction.

